-- Greennest Hub Forum — seed data (OPTIONAL, re-runnable)
--
-- Loads the same 7 topics + 17 replies that shipped with the
-- forum as Markdown files, into public.forum_topics and
-- public.forum_replies. Run AFTER supabase/schema.sql, in the
-- Supabase SQL Editor. Safe to run more than once (ON CONFLICT
-- DO NOTHING) — it never overwrites real user posts.
--
-- The seed rows have author_id NULL (no real account behind
-- them) and author_name/author_location copied from the files.
-- Only the admin can delete them. Real users who sign up later
-- post with their own author_id.

insert into public.forum_topics
  (id, slug, title, category, body, author_id, author_name, author_location, created_at, updated_at)
values
('9acc6e79-6219-5e71-aef0-bdadcf55c8e2', 'best-maize-variety-north-central', 'Which maize variety gives the best yield in the North Central?', 'Crop Problems', 'I farm 3 hectares of maize in Niger State and I want to try a better variety next season. Last season I used a local variety and got about 2 tonnes per hectare, which is too low. I have heard of OBA Super 2, SAMMAZ 15 and SC 645, but I do not know which one does best in our soil and rainfall.

Which variety have you planted in the North Central, and what yield did you get? Also, where did you buy genuine seed? I have been cheated with fake seed before.', NULL, 'Amina', 'Minna, Niger State', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00'),
('2045006e-4858-5d7e-ae62-6492dae5583e', 'best-time-plant-yam-benue', 'Best time to plant yam in Benue — early or late?', 'General', 'Every year I argue with my father about when to plant yam. He says plant early, as soon as the first rains come. My uncle says wait until the rains are steady, or the setts will rot. Last year I planted early and some setts rotted, but the ones that survived gave big tubers.

For Benue farmers, when do you plant your yam, and why? Does early planting really give bigger yam, or is it safer to wait?', NULL, 'Terna', 'Makurdi, Benue State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('79ceb044-789a-55e0-be88-c638e856f1e1', 'broilers-dying-suddenly-4-weeks', 'My broilers are dying suddenly at 4 weeks — please help', 'Livestock', 'I started with 200 broilers and they were fine until week 4. Now 3 to 5 birds die every day. They look dull, stop eating, and some have watery green droppings. I gave them antibiotics from the agro shop but it has not stopped. The pen is dry and I change the litter every week.

What could be killing them? Is it Newcastle disease or coccidiosis? I have already lost 30 birds and I am afraid of losing all. Please, any advice is welcome.', NULL, 'Tunde', 'Abeokuta, Ogun State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('9061ba00-4014-518c-8b2c-0506281b2e16', 'cassava-leaves-curling-yellow', 'My cassava leaves are curling and turning yellow — what is wrong?', 'Crop Problems', 'I planted cassava in April and it was doing well, but for the past three weeks the young leaves are curling up and turning yellow at the edges. Some leaves have white patches too. The stems still look strong, but I am worried the tubers will suffer. I have not sprayed anything yet.

Has anyone seen this before? What is it, and what should I do? I farm about 2 hectares and I do not want to lose the whole crop.', NULL, 'Chinedu', 'Enugu, Enugu State', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00'),
('7cbb6bdd-218b-5a49-9d31-7f7f06c260cd', 'cost-start-small-snail-farm', 'How much does it cost to start a small snail farm?', 'Farm Business', 'I want to start a small snail farm at the back of my house in Ibadan. I have a small space, about half a plot, and I can spend around ₦100,000 to start. I know nothing about snails except that they sell well.

How much did it cost you to start? What do I need — pen, soil, feed, and the snails themselves? How many snails can I start with, and how long before I can sell? Any honest advice will help me decide.', NULL, 'Funke', 'Ibadan, Oyo State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('c044add4-c06a-5956-a7fd-be95f48ef4d2', 'fall-armyworm-eating-maize', 'Fall armyworm is eating my maize — what spray actually works?', 'Pests & Diseases', 'Fall armyworm has attacked my maize badly this season. The caterpillars are inside the whorl of the plants and the leaves are full of holes. I sprayed a chemical my neighbour recommended but the worms are still there after two days.

What spray have you used that really kills fall armyworm? I have heard of neem, ash, and different chemicals. My maize is 5 weeks old. I need something that works fast before they finish the whole farm.', NULL, 'Blessing', 'Zaria, Kaduna State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('461bf00c-6c0a-5493-9fe4-c258496e532b', 'where-sell-50-bags-rice-good-price', 'Where can I sell 50 bags of rice at a good price this month?', 'Market & Prices', 'I have just harvested and milled 50 bags of rice. The middlemen in my town are offering a low price and I know the price is better in Lagos and Onitsha. But transport is expensive and I do not want to carry the rice all the way and still lose money.

Has anyone sold rice to buyers in Lagos or Onitsha recently? What price did you get per bag, and how did you arrange transport? Is it better to sell now or wait a few weeks?', NULL, 'Ibrahim', 'Birnin Kebbi, Kebbi State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

insert into public.forum_replies
  (id, topic_id, body, author_id, author_name, author_location, created_at, updated_at)
values
('6e58176b-ecac-5c0c-a49d-a7539b088893', '9acc6e79-6219-5e71-aef0-bdadcf55c8e2', 'I planted OBA Super 2 last season in Nasarawa and got about 4 tonnes per hectare with good fertilizer and weeding. SAMMAZ 15 is also good and resists striga, which matters if your soil has striga. Buy seed only from a known agro-dealer or the seed company agent — check the pack for the seal and expiry date. Fake seed is the biggest problem, not the variety.', NULL, 'Sule', 'Lafia, Nasarawa State', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00'),
('5f297885-88c7-59b3-802f-ff887afb9c38', '9acc6e79-6219-5e71-aef0-bdadcf55c8e2', 'Thank you Sule. My soil does have striga in some parts, so SAMMAZ 15 sounds right for those plots. I will try OBA Super 2 on the clean plot and SAMMAZ 15 where striga is a problem, then compare the yields myself next season.', NULL, 'Amina', 'Minna, Niger State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('58cffccc-76ea-5253-a20b-330d4bea6808', '2045006e-4858-5d7e-ae62-6492dae5583e', 'Your father is right and your uncle is also right — it depends on the rain. In Benue, I plant as soon as we get two good rains in a row, usually late March or early April. Planting too early before the rains settle rots the setts, but waiting until May gives smaller tubers. The trick: plant when the soil is moist deep down, not just wet on top. Dig and check — if the soil is dry 10cm down, wait.', NULL, 'Doose', 'Gboko, Benue State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('734579b4-747c-56a4-92d4-4115ff8e2f61', '2045006e-4858-5d7e-ae62-6492dae5583e', 'Thank you Doose. That settles the argument in my house — I will check the soil depth this year instead of arguing about dates. I will plant after two good rains and see how the tubers come out.', NULL, 'Terna', 'Makurdi, Benue State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('7e07d0c1-6733-5dcc-bb5b-b1cdc4b363d0', '79ceb044-789a-55e0-be88-c638e856f1e1', 'Green watery droppings and sudden deaths at 4 weeks — stop the antibiotics and call a vet today. It could be Newcastle disease, and antibiotics do not cure a virus. Did the birds get their Newcastle vaccine at day 1 and the booster? If not, vaccinate the remaining healthy birds quickly, separate the sick ones, and disinfect the pen. A vet needs to see a dead bird to confirm — do not guess with drugs from the shop.', NULL, 'Dr. Bisi', 'Ibadan, Oyo State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('1a2244e9-8ee0-5e15-860a-b8b3a2d8934e', '79ceb044-789a-55e0-be88-c638e856f1e1', 'I lost 50 birds the same way before I learned to vaccinate. Now I follow the vaccination schedule strictly: Newcastle at day 1, Gumboro at day 14, Newcastle booster at day 21. Since then, no sudden deaths. Also check your water — dirty water spreads disease fast. Clean the drinkers every day with clean water.', NULL, 'Kemi', 'Ilorin, Kwara State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('8a7a437a-c784-51aa-9d19-acccb0eb3a90', '79ceb044-789a-55e0-be88-c638e856f1e1', 'Update: the vet came and confirmed Newcastle disease. I have separated the sick birds, disinfected the pen, and vaccinated the healthy ones. I lost 45 birds in total, but the rest are stable now. Lesson learned — I will never skip vaccination again. Thank you all for the quick advice.', NULL, 'Tunde', 'Abeokuta, Ogun State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('91a3ee35-6381-5a0c-b16b-cbea95653314', '9061ba00-4014-518c-8b2c-0506281b2e16', 'Curling and yellowing young leaves with white patches sounds like cassava mosaic disease or mealybug. First check the underside of the leaves — if you see tiny white insects, it is mealybug. Remove the worst leaves and burn them far from the farm, do not compost them. Next season, plant only clean cuttings from healthy plants. Do not spray blindly before you know what it is — show a leaf to your extension officer.', NULL, 'Ngozi', 'Awka, Anambra State', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-19T12:00:00+01:00'),
('5d1b6b64-20ce-5fbd-9ed0-a2d50267dc58', '9061ba00-4014-518c-8b2c-0506281b2e16', 'I had the same problem two seasons ago. The tubers still formed, but they were smaller than normal. My advice: do not panic and do not uproot everything. Feed the crop well — apply NPK if you have not — and keep the farm weed-free so the plants can recover. For the white patches, I used a simple soap spray (liquid soap mixed with water) on the leaves and it helped with the insects.', NULL, 'Emeka', 'Owerri, Imo State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('8e1429e7-daea-50df-a7c0-abe5b157330c', '9061ba00-4014-518c-8b2c-0506281b2e16', 'Good advice from Ngozi and Emeka. One more check: if the yellowing starts from the older leaves and moves up, it can also be a nutrient problem — cassava needs potassium. If it starts from the young leaves, it is more likely disease or insects. Either way, take a photo of the leaves to your local agriculture extension office before buying any chemical. You can also read our Safe Crops guides for how to spot the common cassava problems.', NULL, 'Greennest Hub', 'Lagos, Nigeria', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('1e57541e-7564-51cd-89bb-5352c69149f7', '7cbb6bdd-218b-5a49-9d31-7f7f06c260cd', 'I started with ₦80,000 two years ago. My breakdown: pen (wood and net) ₦25,000, good loamy soil and leaves free from my compound, 50 point-of-lay snails at ₦800 each = ₦40,000, feed (pawpaw leaves, cocoyam leaves, maize) about ₦10,000 for the first months. Snails are slow money — mine started laying after 6 months and I sold the first batch after about 10 months. Start small, learn, then grow.', NULL, 'Ada', 'Umuahia, Abia State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('d8b601fa-e3b3-5b5b-ae6d-ee0b3fe59b9e', '7cbb6bdd-218b-5a49-9d31-7f7f06c260cd', 'Ada is right about the money, but do not buy your first snails from the open market — many are old and will not lay. Buy from a known snail farmer, and ask to see the parents laying eggs. Also, snails need shade and moisture always. If your backyard is hot and dry, build the pen under a tree or cover it well, and water the soil every evening. Dry soil kills snails fast.', NULL, 'Segun', 'Akure, Ondo State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('b5244f2c-f42a-5cd1-b879-2d4612276f9d', 'c044add4-c06a-5956-a7fd-be95f48ef4d2', 'The trick is to spray INTO the whorl where the caterpillars hide, not just on the leaves. I use a knapsack sprayer and aim down into the centre of each plant early in the morning. A neem-based spray worked for me when the attack was small. When it is heavy, I use an approved chemical with emamectin benzoate — ask your agro-dealer for the one labelled for fall armyworm and follow the dose on the label exactly.', NULL, 'Yakubu', 'Kano, Kano State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('626dafc7-268e-5f7a-8388-e69ad047ca97', 'c044add4-c06a-5956-a7fd-be95f48ef4d2', 'Do not wait — armyworm can finish a young maize farm in days. I mix wood ash with a little water and pour it into the whorl of each plant; it kills the small caterpillars and costs almost nothing. For a big farm, ash alone is too slow, so combine it: ash on the worst plants today, then spray tomorrow. And plant early next season — early maize escapes the worst of the armyworm.', NULL, 'Hauwa', 'Bauchi, Bauchi State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('5bf0732d-aab0-5479-8cf6-6c93b93eeef2', 'c044add4-c06a-5956-a7fd-be95f48ef4d2', 'Both good answers. One warning: never mix different chemicals together, and never spray more than the label says — it does not kill more worms, it only poisons your soil and your pocket. Spray early morning or late evening when the caterpillars are feeding. Check the plants again after 3 days; if you still see live caterpillars, spray once more.', NULL, 'Greennest Hub', 'Lagos, Nigeria', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00'),
('2da92fb2-160f-5495-9d1c-667526cc7dd7', '461bf00c-6c0a-5493-9fe4-c258496e532b', 'I buy rice for Onitsha market. If your rice is well milled and stone-free, buyers here pay better than the village middlemen. But do not carry 50 bags yourself — transport from Kebbi will eat your profit. First call two or three big buyers in Onitsha, agree a price per bag on the phone, then send a sample of 2 bags by transport. If they like it, they will pay for the rest and arrange the transport themselves.', NULL, 'Chukwu', 'Onitsha, Anambra State', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-20T12:00:00+01:00'),
('ec0253ae-4509-5f0b-a5da-63e20ba9dbcf', '461bf00c-6c0a-5493-9fe4-c258496e532b', 'Thank you Chukwu. I will try the sample idea — I did not know buyers arrange transport themselves. I will also check the market prices page here on Greennest Hub before I agree any price, so I know the current Lagos and Onitsha rates.', NULL, 'Ibrahim', 'Birnin Kebbi, Kebbi State', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00', '2026-11-21T12:00:00+01:00')
on conflict (id) do nothing;

